      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(infra): bound warning dedup caches with createDedupeCache",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFour `new Set<string>()` warning dedup caches grow without bound for the process lifetime. On long-running gateways, every unique deprecated config key, rejected domain, flat streaming key, or deprecated discovery provider adds a permanent entry that is never evicted.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace each unbounded `Set<string>` with `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })`. The `check()` method combines `has()`+`add()` into one size-bounded operation. When the cache exceeds 4096 entries, the oldest half is evicted.\n\nExisting behavior is unchanged: each warning still fires exactly once. Test-only `clear()` helpers continue to work. Follows the same pattern from #101746 and #109000.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLong-running gateways no longer accumulate unbounded memory from one-shot warning dedup caches. Warning behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `src/plugins/provider-validation.ts` — deprecated discovery provider warnings\n- `src/channels/streaming-flat-key-deprecation.ts` — flat streaming key deprecation\n- `src/plugins/runtime/runtime-config.ts` — deprecated config API warnings\n- `src/plugin-sdk/provider-auth.ts` — rejected config domain warnings\n- `pnpm test src/plugins/provider-validation.test.ts src/channels/streaming-flat-key-deprecation.test.ts src/plugins/runtime/runtime-config.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/provider-auth.test.ts` — 43 passed, 0 regressions\n- `pnpm test src/infra/dedupe.test.ts` — createDedupeCache eviction behavior: after maxSize entries, check() evicts oldest half and returns false for new keys, keeping memory bounded",
        "branch": "fix/bound-warning-dedup-caches",
